-- ============================================================================
-- Insert the current iMINT/PIKAS legacy-reversion content (Research/diagnostic_v4_master.csv,
-- 111 items) and its v3/v4 skill taxonomy (Research/skills_taxonomy.csv, 93 skills) as a
-- NEW diagnostic. New rows only -- no existing diagnostics / diagnostic_questions / skills
-- row is modified or deleted, so old sessions keep rendering.
--
-- Root cause this migration fixes: ACTIVE_DIAG_ID (dashboard/lib/diagnostics.ts) has
-- pointed at 'cleanroom-v1' (id ...0002, question_count=67, 36-skill dotted taxonomy)
-- since the clean-room era, but the clean-room approach was abandoned 2026-09-12 in favor
-- of rebuilding on the original iMINT/PIKAS CSVs. The Flutter client has served the new
-- 111-item bank ever since, entirely disconnected from this backend content -- so every
-- session since the pivot has been scored server-side against the wrong, stale diagnostic
-- (auto-completing at 67 answers regardless of the child's actual progress) and the
-- dashboard's server-side Foerderplan generator (foerderplan-generate) has been silently
-- dropping every recommendation whose skill id isn't one of the old 36 dotted ids.
--
-- SLUG / ID: new diagnostic uses slug 'imint-pikas-v4', version 1, fixed uuid
-- 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003 (legacy iMINT row keeps ...0001, cleanroom-v1 keeps ...0002; both frozen).
-- ============================================================================

